IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qda-dates`

-- Taxation Administration Act 2001 (Queensland), as it applies to duty under the Duties Act 2001 -- seat-neutral core:
-- when duty must be paid, unpaid tax interest, penalty tax, objections, and appeals or QCAT review. Section 6(1)
-- makes the Duties Act 2001 a revenue law, and Duties Act s 5 says the two Acts "must be read together as if they
-- together formed a single Act". Written in the Act's own actors and terms (the taxpayer, the commissioner). The buyer's
-- questions are in qda-seat.l4.
--
-- PROVISIONS: ss 13(1)(a)-(b) (as facts), 14A, 26(3), 30(1)(b), (e), (2), 54(1), (2), (5)(aa)(i), (c), (e), (6), (7);
-- 58(1)-(3); 60 (noted); 63(1), (2)(a), 64(1), 65(1)-(2); 67(1), 68(1); 69(1)-(2).
--
-- Edition: Taxation Administration Act 2001 (act-2001-072), the version in force from 2025-02-28 (current on
-- 2026-10-20), as deposited at ../../../taxation-administration-act-2001/registers/source-bundle/act-2001-072.txt.
-- THE PRESCRIBED RATE OF INTEREST (s 54, "the rate prescribed under a regulation") and the weekday on which late
-- payment interest accrues (s 54(3)(b)) are set by the Taxation Administration Regulation 2022, which is NOT deposited:
-- the rate is an input, and the weekly accrual is not encoded.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 2001 (Qld) -- payment, interest, penalty tax and objections for duty`

DECLARE `Tax party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the commissioner`

DECLARE `Tax act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the tax`
    `pay the tax with the unpaid tax interest accrued on it`
    `lodge an objection in writing, stating its grounds in detail, with copies of all relevant material`
    `decide the objection and give the objector written notice of the decision`
    `appeal to the Supreme Court or apply to QCAT for a review` HAS `having paid the whole of the tax and late payment interest` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `s 30 -- when the duty must be paid`

-- s 30(1): "Tax payable under a tax law must be paid-- ... (b) for a standard self assessment--by the date that is 14
-- days after the date the transaction statement for the self assessment is lodged; ... (e) otherwise--by the date stated
-- in the assessment notice as the date by which the tax must be paid." (2): "For subsection (1)(e), the stated date must
-- be at least 30 days after the assessment notice for the tax is given to the taxpayer." s 14A: a self assessor's
-- transaction statement is a standard self assessment.
`the days to pay after a transaction statement is lodged` MEANS 14
`the fewest days an assessment notice must allow for payment` MEANS 30

DECLARE `How the duty is assessed` IS ONE OF
    `by a self assessor lodging a transaction statement`
    `by the commissioner giving an assessment notice`

DECLARE `Payment answer` IS ONE OF
    `the duty must be paid by` HAS `the due date` IS A DATE
    `the notice states a date less than 30 days after it was given, which s 30(2) does not allow; 30 days after it was given is` HAS `the earliest date the notice could state` IS A DATE

GIVEN `how assessed`                            IS A `How the duty is assessed`
      `the day the transaction statement was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day the assessment notice was given`  IS A DATE
      `the date stated in the assessment notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`the s 30 time for payment` `how assessed` `the day the transaction statement was lodged` `the day the assessment notice was given` `the date stated in the assessment notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how assessed`
    WHEN `by a self assessor lodging a transaction statement` THEN
        `the duty must be paid by` (`the day that is` `the days to pay after a transaction statement is lodged` `days after` `the day the transaction statement was lodged`)
    WHEN `by the commissioner giving an assessment notice` THEN
        IF `is before` `the date stated in the assessment notice` `the 30th day`
        THEN `the notice states a date less than 30 days after it was given, which s 30(2) does not allow; 30 days after it was given is` `the 30th day`
        ELSE `the duty must be paid by` `the date stated in the assessment notice`
    WHERE
        `the 30th day` MEANS `the day that is` `the fewest days an assessment notice must allow for payment` `days after` `the day the assessment notice was given`

-- s 30 with s 54: the tax must be paid in the days allowed; if it is not, it must still be paid, now with unpaid tax
-- interest (s 54(1): "A taxpayer must pay interest ... on the amount of primary tax ... unpaid from time to time"), which
-- has no further deadline. Clock: days from the assessment (the notice given, or the transaction statement lodged).
GIVEN `the days allowed to pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Tax party` `Tax act`
DECIDE `ss 30, 54(1) -- the taxpayer must pay by the due date, and after it must pay with unpaid tax interest` IS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    MUST   `pay the tax`
    WITHIN `the days allowed to pay`
    LEST
        PARTY `the taxpayer`
        MUST  `pay the tax with the unpaid tax interest accrued on it`

§§ `s 54 -- unpaid tax interest`

-- s 54(2): "Unpaid tax interest, other than late payment interest, accrues daily at the prescribed rate on the unpaid
-- primary tax for the period starting on the start date and ending on the date the primary tax is paid in full, both
-- dates inclusive." (5): the start date is the day after "(aa) for a standard self assessment--(i) the due date ...";
-- "(c) for another original assessment--(i) the due date for the assessment; or (ii) if the taxpayer has not complied with
-- 1 or more information or lodgement requirements for the assessment--the date that is the same number of days before
-- the due date for the assessment as the number of days in the periods of noncompliance"; "(e) for a reassessment of
-- another original assessment--the date mentioned in paragraph (b) or (c) for the assessment" (so interest on a
-- reassessment runs from the original start date). (6)(b): "the date on which the requirement is complied with is
-- included in calculating a period of noncompliance". (7)(a): for a reassessment, the unpaid primary tax is the
-- reassessed primary tax that is unpaid.
-- The (7) example: $10,000 at "10% per year", 13 April to 24 April inclusive, gives "$32.87": daily accrual is the annual
-- rate over 365 days, and the example drops the part of a cent (10,000 x 10% x 12 / 365 = 32.8767). That is the only
-- rounding the text shows, and the encoding follows it. Late payment interest under a revenue law accrues weekly on a
-- prescribed day (s 54(3)(b)); that timing is not encoded (the regulation is not deposited).
`the days in a year for daily interest` MEANS 365

GIVEN `the day the requirement had to be met` IS A DATE
      `the day it was met`                     IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of noncompliance from` `the day the requirement had to be met` `to` `the day it was met` MEANS
    `the days from` `the day the requirement had to be met` `until` `the day it was met`

GIVEN `the due date`                IS A DATE
      `the days of noncompliance`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the start date for unpaid tax interest` `the due date` `the days of noncompliance` MEANS
    `the day that is` 1 `days after` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the due date` MINUS `the days of noncompliance`))

GIVEN `the unpaid primary tax`     IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed rate`        IS A NUMBER
      `the start date`             IS A DATE
      `the date paid in full`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unpaid tax interest on` `the unpaid primary tax` `at` `the prescribed rate` `from` `the start date` `to` `the date paid in full` MEANS
    IF `the days` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR (`the unpaid primary tax` TIMES `the prescribed rate` TIMES `the days` DIVIDED BY `the days in a year for daily interest` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the days` MEANS `the number of days from` `the start date` `to` `the date paid in full` `both inclusive`

§§ `s 58 -- penalty tax`

-- s 58(1): "A taxpayer is liable for an amount (penalty tax) if-- (a) the commissioner makes a default assessment under
-- section 13(1)(a) or (b); or (b) the commissioner makes a reassessment and the original assessment was a default
-- assessment under section 13(1)(a) or (b); or (c) the primary tax assessed on a reassessment, other than under a
-- reassessment mentioned in paragraph (b), is more than the primary tax assessed on the original assessment or an earlier
-- reassessment." (2): (a) 75% of the primary tax assessed; (b) 75% of the reassessed primary tax; "(c) if subsection (1)(c)
-- applies and the primary tax assessed on the last reassessment is more than the primary tax assessed on the original
-- assessment--an amount equal to 75% of the difference"; "(d) if ... less than the primary tax assessed on the original
-- assessment but more than the primary tax assessed on an earlier reassessment--... 75% of the difference between the
-- primary tax assessed on the last reassessment and the lowest primary tax assessed on an earlier reassessment". (3):
-- "The commissioner may increase the amount of the penalty tax by not more than 20% ... if the commissioner is satisfied
-- the taxpayer-- (a) has not complied with section 28; or (b) has hindered or prevented the commissioner from becoming
-- aware of the nature and extent of the taxpayer's liability". s 60(1): "The commissioner may remit the whole or part"
-- (a judgment left to the commissioner: the amounts here are before any remission).
-- s 13(1)(a)-(b) (no self assessment made, or a document or information not lodged or given; or the commissioner not
-- satisfied with what was lodged) is a FACT.
`the penalty tax rate` MEANS 75%
`the most the penalty tax may be increased` MEANS 20%

DECLARE `Penalty tax` HAS
    `penalty tax under s 58(2)`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the most it may be increased to under s 58(3)` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `it is a default assessment under s 13(1)(a) or (b), or a reassessment of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the primary tax assessed`                            IS A NUMBER
      `the primary tax on the original assessment`          IS A NUMBER
      `the lowest primary tax on an earlier reassessment`   IS A NUMBER
      `the commissioner is satisfied s 58(3)(a) or (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty tax`
`the penalty tax for` `it is a default assessment under s 13(1)(a) or (b), or a reassessment of one` `the primary tax assessed` `the primary tax on the original assessment` `the lowest primary tax on an earlier reassessment` `the commissioner is satisfied s 58(3)(a) or (b) applies` MEANS
    `Penalty tax` WITH
        `penalty tax under s 58(2)` IS `the base`
        `the most it may be increased to under s 58(3)` IS
            IF `the commissioner is satisfied s 58(3)(a) or (b) applies`
            THEN `the base` PLUS (`the base` TIMES `the most the penalty tax may be increased`)
            ELSE `the base`
    WHERE
        `the base` MEANS
            IF `it is a default assessment under s 13(1)(a) or (b), or a reassessment of one`
            THEN `the penalty tax rate` TIMES `the primary tax assessed`
            ELSE IF `the primary tax assessed` GREATER THAN `the primary tax on the original assessment`
                 THEN `the penalty tax rate` TIMES (`the primary tax assessed` MINUS `the primary tax on the original assessment`)
                 ELSE IF `the primary tax assessed` GREATER THAN `the lowest primary tax on an earlier reassessment`
                      THEN `the penalty tax rate` TIMES (`the primary tax assessed` MINUS `the lowest primary tax on an earlier reassessment`)
                      ELSE 0

§§ `ss 63-69 -- objections, and appeals or QCAT review`

-- s 63(1): "A taxpayer who is dissatisfied with an original assessment, other than a compromise assessment, may object";
-- (2)(a) also to "a reassessment increasing the taxpayer's liability"; s 64(1): "on any grounds". s 65(1): "An objection
-- must-- (a) be in writing; and (b) state in detail the grounds ...; and (c) be accompanied by copies of all material
-- relevant to decide the objection; and (d) be lodged within 60 days after ... the assessment notice ... is given";
-- (2): the commissioner "may extend the time" if satisfied 60 days would be unreasonable (a judgment, not encoded).
-- s 67(1): "The commissioner must allow the objection completely or partly or disallow it." s 68(1): the commissioner
-- "must give written notice to the objector". s 69(1): the right applies if the taxpayer "is dissatisfied with the
-- commissioner's decision" and "(b) for an objection under section 63--the taxpayer has paid the whole of the amount of
-- the tax and late payment interest payable under the assessment"; (2): "within 60 days after notice is given ... of the
-- commissioner's decision-- (a) appeal to the Supreme Court; or (b) apply ... to QCAT for a review". (3): QCAT may not
-- extend that period. The Act sets no time for the commissioner's decision.
-- Objecting and appealing are choices, so not taking them is no breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED). The nested rules are
-- bracketed: unbracketed, the stable l4 attaches the last LEST to the commissioner's rule. Clock: days from the
-- assessment notice; the appeal clock runs from the decision notice.
`the days to object` MEANS 60
`the days to appeal or apply for review` MEANS 60

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Tax party` `Tax act`
DECIDE `ss 63-69 -- the taxpayer may object within 60 days, the commissioner must decide, and the taxpayer may then appeal or seek review within 60 days, having paid` IS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    DO     `lodge an objection in writing, stating its grounds in detail, with copies of all relevant material`
    WITHIN `the days to object`
    HENCE
        (PARTY `the commissioner`
         MUST  `decide the objection and give the objector written notice of the decision`
         HENCE
             (PARTY  `the taxpayer`
              DO     `appeal to the Supreme Court or apply to QCAT for a review` `paid` PROVIDED `paid`
              WITHIN `the days to appeal or apply for review`
              LEST   FULFILLED))
    LEST   FULFILLED

GIVEN `the day the assessment notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object to an assessment notice given on` `the day the assessment notice was given` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the days to object` `days after` `the day the assessment notice was given`

DECLARE `Appeal answer` IS ONE OF
    `an appeal or application for QCAT review may be made up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not yet: the whole of the tax and late payment interest must be paid first, and the 60 days end on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the day the objection decision notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the whole of the tax and late payment interest is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Appeal answer`
`the s 69 right of appeal or review` `the day the objection decision notice was given` `the whole of the tax and late payment interest is paid` MEANS
    IF `the whole of the tax and late payment interest is paid`
    THEN `an appeal or application for QCAT review may be made up to and including` `the last day`
    ELSE `not yet: the whole of the tax and late payment interest must be paid first, and the 60 days end on` `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the day that is` `the days to appeal or apply for review` `days after` `the day the objection decision notice was given`
